From a550d08076680af4bd287466a4f6ea1e48a6b49a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pieroviano <piero.viano@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 07:40:52 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Phase 3 (additive): ToolStrip containers, renderers,
 ProfessionalColorTable

Adds the ToolStrip theming and container surface without touching the control
hierarchy. All signatures/values taken from the net48 reference assembly.

Designer-emitted container controls (compile breaks on generated multi-toolbar
forms):
- ToolStripContainer : ContainerControl (Top/Bottom/Left/Right ToolStripPanel +
  ContentPanel + visibility flags), ToolStripPanel : ContainerControl
  (Orientation/Renderer/RenderMode/Rows), ToolStripContentPanel : Panel,
  ToolStripPanelRow. Backed by existing PanelBase widgets.

Theming (compiling shims over GTK theming):
- ProfessionalColorTable (56 colors from SystemColors) + ProfessionalColors.
- ToolStripRenderer with 20 public Draw* methods each dispatching to a protected
  virtual OnRender* override point; ToolStripProfessionalRenderer (+ColorTable)
  and ToolStripSystemRenderer. Base render methods are no-ops since GTK draws the
  chrome; custom-renderer overrides are still invoked (verified).
- ToolStripManager (Renderer/RenderMode/VisualStylesEnabled/Merge/RevertMerge).
- The 9 ToolStrip render event args + their delegate handlers.

Deliberately NOT done here: re-parenting ToolStripDropDown from ToolStripItem to
ToolStrip. That control is backed by a GTK menu (StripDropDown/IToolMenuItem),
not a Control widget, and ContextMenuStrip/ToolStripDropDownMenu build on it; the
surgery would risk destabilizing the working menu system and is deferred.

Net48 public types present 571->599 (missing 463->435). Full suite green at 2311
(+9 tests: color-table/ProfessionalColors delegation, renderer Draw->OnRender
wiring, ToolStripManager, render-arg round-trips, container panel behaviour).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
